      "mergeID": "666853434aee560d44db52bb",
      "mergedPostDetails": "When setting an avatar as a fallback on both Quest and PC, there's an unexpected requirement: all other avatars in the scene must be disabled.\n\nSteps to Reproduce:\n\n    - Upload an avatar to both PC and Quest with a good rating and no validation issues.\n\n    - Ensure other avatars are active in the scene.\n\n    - Attempt to set the selected avatar as the fallback avatar.\n\nExpected Behavior:\n\nThe avatar should be accepted as a fallback if it meets the requirements.\n\nActual Behavior:\n\n    - A prompt appears: \"This avatar cannot be used as a fallback. Check validations below for more info.\"\n\n    - The issue occurs only when other avatars are active in the scene.\n\n    - In Windows build mode, the avatar is indicated as valid for fallback and suggests switching to Android build mode to set it.\n\nIt's unclear if this requirement to disable other avatars is intentional. If it is, it may be good to have a validation message about this to make it more clear why the option isn't showing up.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[VRChat SDK - Avatars 3.6.1] Can not set valid fallback avatar as fallback unless all other avatars in the scene are disabled",
